-gY295K0Rci_xozVXfdMkSQTLW6cwJThYulHEtVjXrGTiVgSzBrwjw9JHoi2ZXIayQBrWC3wfnMLF7rkFqXa8Fplpd9b1wM7cYNFlzudPt8MrMdzvSSRZAXJqFA5bf2_Xwc58vdRqm5YYms9TUllNaIy49dJ2Ae5aPMI4EDuR_-FEDBczWk-YWA469ZRX9mDyYssgenN-RV7YeFa-reV3A4kvyPtU-hjJ9QF6QxHzZxQdENP7QWknY8cTs752OUlgRxi-gYJSSFPgfogQ..&amp;amp;type=2&amp;amp;query=%E6%BF%80%E5%85%89%E9%9B%B7%E8%BE%BE&amp;amp;token=4A05567023A0188101075AD1F7C405700186DEFC6AAE4A79</link><description>激光雷达凭借厘米级三维感知能力,被视为高阶智驾不可或缺的关键传感器;与此同时,纯视觉方案的崛起、多传感器融合趋势的深化...</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bc0d80b1a842</guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T08:40:32.115401+00:00</pubDate><source>搜狗微信·光电行业 · 迪普战略研究所</source><category>激光</category></item><item><title>On-chip space–time wave packet laser array</title><link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41566-026-02003-0</link><description>Nature Photonics, Published online: 11 September 2026; doi:10.1038/s41566-026-02003-0 An integrated semiconductor laser array can directly generate incoherent space–time wave packets with propagation-invariant and self-healing characteristics.</description><guid isPermaLink="false">b2dd1d08f139</guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T08:40:32.115401+00:00</pubDate><source>Nature Photonics</source><category>激光</category></item><item><title>Laser experiments recreate solar flare physics and reveal consistent magnetic reconnection rates</title><link>https://phys.org/news/2026-09-laser-recreate-solar-flare-physics.html</link><description>Magnetic reconnection is a process that occurs when the magnetic fields of a conductive plasma quickly rearrange and release massive amounts of stored magnetic energy. It is widely thought to be the underlying mechanism behind cosmic events such as solar flares and substorms in Earth's magnetosphere.</description><guid isPermaLink="false">fb7b5931e69e</guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T08:40:32.115401+00:00</pubDate><source>Phys.org 物理新闻</source><category>激光</category></item><item><title>Speedy electrons for brilliant laser light: Research paves the way for compact, inexpensive free-electron lasers</title><link>https://phys.org/news/2026-09-speedy-electrons-brilliant-laser-paves.html</link><description>Extremely short, intense light flashes are in high demand to investigate atoms, molecules and new materials. Free-electron lasers (FELs) produce these flashes. But around the world, beam time available at large-scale user facilities is in short supply, and waiting times are long.</description><guid isPermaLink="false">e0210801bb0d</guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T08:40:32.115401+00:00</pubDate><source>Phys.org 物理新闻</source><category>激光</category></item></channel></rss>